{# DEPARTMENTS — the area-aware manager (the register).

   PORTED from the canonical design DesignsProjects/uhifadhi-web/departments/
   index.html: area-linked departments first, grouped under their area's name,
   then org-wide; an explicit SCOPE column on every row; create per-area (the
   picker enumerates the installation's areas through the contract) OR per-org,
   area-first because it is the correctable choice; and the audited scope change
   — confine to an area, or promote to org-wide, a reason required. Every row
   opens the department's own lens through its name and its Lens action.

   DEACTIVATE is drawn as the design's per-row danger action: it flips the
   department's active flag (deactivate, never delete), the footprint informs
   without guarding, and a deactivated row reads greyed with a Reactivate action.

   WHAT THE DESIGN DRAWS THAT IS THE RICH-LENS FOLLOW-UP, and so not here yet:
   the Widgets button in the header (the department's widget board). #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiShell/page.html.twig' %}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/positions/_bits.html.twig' as pm %}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/departments/_bits.html.twig' as di %}

{% block title %}Departments{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_tabs %}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('team_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / departments
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Departments{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    Every department the organisation has. Each is either <b>area-linked</b> &mdash; belonging to one area &mdash;
    or <b>org-wide</b>, spanning every area. Area-linked come first here; each row states its scope. A department
    shapes emphasis and holds the positions its people fill; <b>it never gates data</b>. Open a department&rsquo;s own
    <b>lens</b> from its name or the <b>Lens</b> action; the manager itself stays a management list.
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {% set hasAreas = areas|length > 0 %}
    <div data-dp>
        {# CREATE — the scope question first (area-first by default, the narrow
           correctable choice), then the name, and for an area, which one. #}
        <form class="crcard" method="post" action="{{ path('team_department_create') }}"
              data-controller="uhifadhi--team-module--department"
              data-scope="{{ hasAreas ? 'area' : 'org' }}"
              data-create-department
              data-uhifadhi--team-module--department-hint-area-value="<b>Just an area.</b> This department will belong only to the area you pick above and will not appear in the others &mdash; the safer default, and easy to widen later."
              data-uhifadhi--team-module--department-hint-org-value="<b>Org-wide.</b> This department will belong to the organisation and appear in every area as an inherited department.">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="scope" value="{{ hasAreas ? 'area' : 'org' }}"
                   data-uhifadhi--team-module--department-target="scopeField">
            <div class="crgrid">
                <div class="crfield">
                    <span class="crlab">Scope &mdash; just this area, or org-wide?</span>
                    <div class="seg" role="tablist">
                        <button type="button" class="{{ hasAreas ? 'on' : '' }}" data-scope-set="area"
                                {{ hasAreas ? '' : 'disabled' }}
                                data-uhifadhi--team-module--department-target="segment"
                                data-action="uhifadhi--team-module--department#setScope">{{ di.icon_area() }} Just an area</button>
                        <button type="button" class="{{ hasAreas ? '' : 'on' }}" data-scope-set="org"
                                data-uhifadhi--team-module--department-target="segment"
                                data-action="uhifadhi--team-module--department#setScope">{{ di.icon_org() }} Org-wide</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="crfield crpick">
                    <span class="crlab">Which area?</span>
                    <select name="area" aria-label="Area">
                        {% for area in areas %}
                            <option value="{{ area.uuidString }}">{{ area.name }}</option>
                        {% else %}
                            <option value="">No areas yet</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                </div>
                <div class="crfield grow">
                    <span class="crlab">Name</span>
                    <input type="text" class="fld" name="name" placeholder="New department"
                           aria-label="New department name" required>
                </div>
                <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ pm.icon_plus() }} Add department</button>
            </div>
            <div class="crhint">
                {{ pm.icon_info() }}
                <span data-uhifadhi--team-module--department-target="hint">
                    {% if hasAreas %}
                        <b>Just an area.</b> This department will belong only to the area you pick above and will not
                        appear in the others &mdash; the safer default, and easy to widen later.
                    {% else %}
                        <b>Org-wide.</b> There are no areas yet, so a department can only be organisation-wide for now.
                        It will belong to the organisation and appear in every area.
                    {% endif %}
                </span>
            </div>
        </form>

        {% set anyDepartments = areaGroups|length > 0 or orgDepartments|length > 0 %}

        {% if not anyDepartments %}
            <div class="pm-first">
                {{ pm.icon_plus() }}
                <div class="ft">
                    <h3>There are no departments yet, and the field above is what makes the first one.</h3>
                    <p>Until one exists, every position on this installation belongs to nobody in particular: the
                    roster&rsquo;s org chart bands them all as <b>Unassigned</b>. A department is an organizational
                    fact, so an installation that has not decided on one yet is simply an installation that has not
                    decided. Three or four is usually the whole list.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {# ── AREA-LEVEL FIRST, grouped by area, then org-level. ── #}
        {% for group in areaGroups %}
            <div class="deptgroup">
                <span class="gh">Area-level &middot; {{ group.area.name }}</span>
                <span class="gc">{{ group.departments|length }}</span>
                <span class="gnote">Belong to this one area</span>
                <span class="gl"></span>
            </div>
            {% for department in group.departments %}
                {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/departments/_row.html.twig', {
                    department: department,
                    positions: owned[department.uuidString]|default([]),
                    people: headcount[department.uuidString]|default(0),
                    holders: holders,
                    fileTargets: fileTargets,
                    areas: areas,
                    mark: marks[department.uuidString]|default('—'),
                    csrfToken: csrfToken,
                }, with_context: false) }}
            {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}

        {% if orgDepartments|length %}
            <div class="deptgroup">
                <span class="gh">Org-level</span>
                <span class="gc">{{ orgDepartments|length }}</span>
                <span class="gnote">Belong to the organisation &middot; span every area</span>
                <span class="gl"></span>
            </div>
            {% for department in orgDepartments %}
                {{ include('@UhifadhiTeam/departments/_row.html.twig', {
                    department: department,
                    positions: owned[department.uuidString]|default([]),
                    people: headcount[department.uuidString]|default(0),
                    holders: holders,
                    fileTargets: fileTargets,
                    areas: areas,
                    mark: marks[department.uuidString]|default('—'),
                    csrfToken: csrfToken,
                }, with_context: false) }}
            {% endfor %}
        {% endif %}

        {# THE LOOSE POSITIONS — every position nobody has filed. Not a department:
           a position may be created before anybody decided which part of the
           organisation owns it, and its holders read as Unassigned until one is
           chosen. The register states this in words so it is never read as a
           department called "No department yet". #}
        {% if loose|length %}
            <div class="deptgroup">
                <span class="gh">No department yet</span>
                <span class="gc">{{ loose|length }}</span>
                <span class="gnote">Not a department &mdash; positions nobody has filed</span>
                <span class="gl"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="posfile" data-unfiled style="border-top:1px solid var(--c-ln);border-radius:12px">
                <p class="aa-prose" style="margin:2px 0 6px">This is <b>not a department</b>. Each position below
                    reads as <b>Unassigned</b> on the roster until you file it &mdash; pick a department in its Move
                    control.</p>
                {% for position in loose %}
                    {% set held = holders[position.uuidString]|default(0) %}
                    <div class="posline">
                        <span class="pl-nm"><a href="{{ path('team_positions', {position: position.uuidString}) }}">{{ position.name }}</a></span>
                        <span class="pl-mem">
                            {%- if held %}{{ held }} holder{{ held == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                            {%- else %}nobody yet{% endif %}
                            &middot; {{ position.permissionValues|length }} permission{{ position.permissionValues|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                        </span>
                        <span class="pl-act">
                            <form class="moveform" method="post" action="{{ path('team_department_file', {uuid: position.uuidString}) }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                                <span class="mlab">File under</span>
                                <select name="department" aria-label="File {{ position.name }} under">
                                    <option value="" selected>No department yet&hellip;</option>
                                    {% for d in fileTargets %}
                                        <option value="{{ d.uuidString }}">{{ d.name }}{{ d.area ? ' · ' ~ d.area.name : '' }}</option>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </select>
                                <button class="softbtn" type="submit">Move</button>
                            </form>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
